{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Geometry",
    "description": "Standard-library polygon-overlap templates (esm-spec §9.7.1 template-library file). Match-less expression templates giving the pure-AST overlap area of two convex polygons, the quantity the `polygon_intersection_area` geometry leaf returns (esm-spec §8.6.1). `overlap_area_planar(ring_a, cell_a, nv_a, ring_b, cell_b, nv_b)` takes two `[cells, verts, 2]` lon-lat (or x-y) ring stacks and returns the area with straight edges, in squared coordinate units (the leaf's `planar` manifold). `overlap_area_spherical(ring_a, cell_a, nv_a, ring_b, cell_b, nv_b)` takes two `[cells, verts, 3]` stacks of unit vectors and returns the area with great-circle edges, in steradians (the leaf's `spherical` and `geodesic` manifolds); `lonlat_to_unit(ring, cell, vert, comp)` gives component `comp` of the unit vector of a lon-lat vertex in degrees, so a caller builds the unit-vector stack once per cell with a `faq`. `cell` is the cell index and `nv` the number of vertex slots (an integer used as a `faq` `ranges` bound, esm-spec §9.6.1). Rings close implicitly, may run either way round, and may carry repeated vertices (an explicit closing duplicate or rectangular-storage padding): a zero-length edge contributes exactly zero and constrains nothing. By Green's theorem the overlap area is the sum over every edge of each polygon of its shoelace (planar) or signed spherical-triangle (spherical, Van Oosterom-Strackee) contribution restricted to the part inside the other polygon; for convex polygons that part is one chord-parameter interval, a `max`/`min` `faq` over the other polygon's closed half-planes. An edge shared by both polygons is counted once, by `ring_a`, when the two run the same way, and not at all when they run opposite ways. Import with `expression_template_imports` and invoke with `apply_expression_template`; see docs/content/standard_library.md.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-07T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "standard-library",
      "geometry",
      "conservative-regridding",
      "polygon_intersection_area",
      "expression-templates"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "esm-spec.md §8.6.1 (the polygon_intersection_area leaf, operand rings, padding); §9.6 (expression templates); §9.7.1 (template-library files); CONFORMANCE_SPEC.md §5.8 (geometry tolerance contract)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Van Oosterom, A. and Strackee, J. (1983). The solid angle of a plane triangle. IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering BME-30(2), 125-126.",
        "doi": "10.1109/TBME.1983.325207"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "overlap_area_planar": {
      "params": [
        "ring_a",
        "cell_a",
        "nv_a",
        "ring_b",
        "cell_b",
        "nv_b"
      ],
      "description": "Overlap area of two convex polygons with straight edges in the plane: cell `cell_a` of the `[cells, nv_a, 2]` ring stack `ring_a` and cell `cell_b` of `ring_b` (vertex v = [x, y], e.g. [lon, lat]). The value of `polygon_intersection_area` with `manifold: \"planar\"` within the esm-spec §8.6.1 / CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.8.2 tolerance. Either ring orientation; repeated vertices contribute exactly zero. Contributions are taken about the first vertex of `ring_a`, so translating both polygons together changes the result only by rounding. A half-plane test within 1e-12 x L1(edge) x (L1(edge start) + L1(edge end) + L1(half-plane edge start)) of zero counts as on the line, which is what makes shared edges and vertices exact. Disjoint or edge-touching polygons give 0. Non-convex input is outside the contract.",
      "body": {"op":"ifelse","args":[{"op":"or","args":[{"op":"==","args":[{"op":"faq","args":["ring_a","ring_b"],"output_idx":[],"reduce":"+","ranges":{"k_overlap_area_planar_1":[1,"nv_a"]},"expr":{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"*","args":[{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a","k_overlap_area_planar_1",1]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a",1,1]}]},{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a",{"op":"ifelse","args":[{"op":"<","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_1","nv_a"]},{"op":"+","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_1",1]},1]},2]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a",1,2]}]}]},{"op":"*","args":[{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a","k_overlap_area_planar_1",2]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a",1,2]}]},{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a",{"op":"ifelse","args":[{"op":"<","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_1","nv_a"]},{"op":"+","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_1",1]},1]},1]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_a","cell_a",1,1]}]}]}]}},0]},{"op":"==","args":[{"op":"faq","args":["ring_a","ring_b"],"output_idx":[],"reduce":"+","ranges":{"k_overlap_area_planar_2":[1,"nv_b"]},"expr":{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"*","args":[{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b","k_overlap_area_planar_2",1]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b",1,1]}]},{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b",{"op":"ifelse","args":[{"op":"<","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_2","nv_b"]},{"op":"+","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_2",1]},1]},2]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b",1,2]}]}]},{"op":"*","args":[{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b","k_overlap_area_planar_2",2]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b",1,2]}]},{"op":"-","args":[{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b",{"op":"ifelse","args":[{"op":"<","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_2","nv_b"]},{"op":"+","args":["k_overlap_area_planar_2",1]},1]},1]},{"op":"index","args":["ring_b","cell_b",1,1]}]}]}]}},0]}]},0,{"op":"+","args":[{"op":"faq",